//   diff-ruN   `diff -ruN a/F b/F`, then Apple `diff -u` with labels `a/F<TAB>mtime` and `b/F<TAB>mtime`; the missing
//              side of a new or deleted file is GNU diff's epoch label, which git reads as no file.
//   unified    Apple `diff -u` with labels a/F and b/F (/dev/null for a missing side).
// order: path (sorted by path: git's index order, `find | sort`), tree (directory by directory: `diff -r`,
//   `git diff --no-index` of two directories), committed (as the committed patch has them, new files last, by path).
